silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_01_reader_onboarding_sections_01_what_the_encyclopedia_is_concrete_anchor_10#mittenssleepingprocess silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensSleepingProcess is the afternoon sleeping process of Mittens on the windowsill: 167-minute duration measurement. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'SleepingProcess(Mittens)', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
